Z||000002||Slammed Fiero||06-22-2001||12:12 PM||||I had this girlfriend one time ..she lived far far away in Ohio.<P>I went there last summer for 2 weeks to see her. My last day she gave me directions home.<BR>a long detailed set of directions<P>I forget the highway #'s , but she told me to take  # xxx West....<P><BR>So I take it , 2 hours later , I get to the end of the highway. Hmmm... I live  East. DOH!. So all the way back through her town I go. 4 hours driving and I'm still in the same place.<P>Then I take highway upon highway until Im suppose to get to 79 north. being tired I miss the exit and keep driving.<P>By this time my newly tinted rear taillight lense had fallen off.. I stoped at one rest stop it was there..the next it wasn't. So I was in a good mood.<P>I drive all the way across Ohio , New york and half way across pennsylvania. I get near harrisburg... DOH... Turn around head for highway 79 in NYS<P>So I'm in BUTT F*CK no where. Canada is north ..can't go wrong heading north. I eventually found Buffalo NY. At 1 in the morning. I left ohio at noon. So lets see.. thats 13 hours...usually a 4 hour trip.<P>So I fianlly get to the border , I get across and get caught in a traffic jam in Toronto at 2:30 in the morning , due to night construction.<BR>We get out of that.. (I race a V6 accord and beat him , highlight of the night)<BR>I head home and at about 4 or so , 18 hours after i left. I only stopped for gas and to buy a map ...I need to learn how to read maps.<P>Next morning both my foglights for some reason are smashed , the car has 10000000 bugs on it. I had to wash it 3 times to get all the crap off.<P>On the upside , I beat that riced out lowered decal accord , My car started getting great gas milage (don't ask me why) and my trip to Ohio was a lot of fun.<P>The "navigator" will remain nameless ..right Lisa? haha<BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">      <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals. &lt;b&gt; New White Face Gauges , 75Hp Shot of NOS&lt;/b&gt;Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||06-22-2001||01:16 PM||||Fourteen hours from Wisconsin Dells to NY arriving home at 2AM..  Not again..a two day trip now. 845 miles is too much.||||reg||1
Z||000004||ChadMan||06-22-2001||01:31 PM||||Longest trip with only fuel and restroom breaks was Columbus to Daytona Beach in the 88 Coupe.  14 hours one way.  On the way home, I found out that driving tired can be just as bad as driving drunk when I didn't see a red light in Charleston, WV and nearly caused an accident.  Thank God those Mountaineers were paying attention.<P>Longest trip period was Columbus to Phoenix in father-in-law's 86 SE.  29 hours of actual drive time, but we took five days to do it!<P>Fieros are GREAT road trip cars IMHO.||||reg||14
Z||000005||DRH||06-22-2001||01:38 PM||||My wife and I took my Formula back to her hometown once, about 700 miles in about 10-11 hours each way for a long weekend. We've made that trip SEVERAL times in the last few years in other cars. The Fiero was really no less comfortable than any other car we've made it with except there's no back seat to stretch out and take a REAL nap...||||reg||1
Z||000006||Alex4mula||06-22-2001||01:44 PM||||29 hrs?? Mmmm. I'm considering a trip from Tucson to West Palm in Florida. There's a nice GT there that I may buy. May be cheaper (& more fun) than shipping the car here.<BR>My longest trip was just a 5 hr drive from West Palm to Key West. I just wish my car had cruise control  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Alex4mula<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p69fbfe3e99ec5a0b81c10afcc578ff95/fe6d5c42.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||06-22-2001||02:14 PM||||from columbus, ohio to dallas tex, then back the next day. it was fun, had some really fast moments  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||LT1 Chop Top||06-22-2001||03:09 PM||||1300+ miles from Barrington Chicago (V8 Archie's) to my home in San Antonio Texas in ~20 hours.  Purred like a kitten.||||reg||1
Z||000009||TI_3VOM||06-22-2001||03:32 PM||||(in my first Fiero, a silver '85 GT 4spd, w/no AC)....From Loring Air Force Base, in northern Maine (aka occupied Canada), through Canada, to Chicago. Straight through, I estimated it would've taken me 24-28 hours. Instead, I overnighted in Quebec, then London, Ontario the next day. Made it home in 2 1/2 days. <BR>Best part: the drive between Quebec and London. The roads were so free of traffic and construction that I just floored that V-6 till the needle on the 85mph speedo came back around to 5mph (geee...how fast is that?) :P<BR>Worst part: Merging back onto the highway after fueling up outside of London, accelerating to speed, and watching the drivers' side windshield wiper depart the arm and fly off, and then later run into rain as I enter Indiana (thank god for Rain-X).  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||mrfiero||06-22-2001||04:11 PM||||The longest non stop trip for me was from Denver, CO to Groton, CT (about 2000 miles).  This was 10 years ago while I was in the Navy (stationed in Groton) in my first Fiero.....an '88 GT.  It took me about 40 hours when all was said and done.<P>The longest road trip I ever took was last year.....Denver to Portland, OR to Portland, ME to Detroit, MI back to Denver.  For 75% of the trip I was towing another car! This was in another '88 GT.  I believe that trip was over the 6000 mile mark and I did it in a week.||||reg||1
Z||000011||CoolBlue87GT||06-22-2001||04:59 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DecadenceR:<BR><B>What is the longest trip that you have taken straight through, only restroom and fuel up stops, in your Fiero</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>17.5 hours with my 84 sport 4 cly.  Washington to Punta Gorda, Fl a few years ago.<P>Just recently 21.5 hours returning from the Carlisle show to Punta Gorda, Fl w/my 87 GT<P>- oh, wait, you said "in your Fiero". - that 21.5 hours was towing it !<P>Well, it was a long drive anyway.  Thank goodness for cruise control.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000012||Ken Wittlief||06-22-2001||05:10 PM||||Ive noticed there is a point, right around 2 hours or so, after which your brain says, this is boring - Im outta here - and you mentally zone out.<P>  after that point it doesnt seem to matter how much longer you drive - its all a blur after that.<P>  when you start singing Christmas Carols in august at 3am (and are having a great time) then you know you are totally brain dead.||||reg||1
Z||000013||SteveJ||06-22-2001||05:25 PM||||658 miles from Buffalo NY to Urbanna IL in 10 hours. <P>The TCC quit at a toll barrier and hour and a half into the trip but because of PENNOCKS's FIERO FORUM  I knew which plug to pull right there on the spot. It saved the trip and saved the cost of a service call.||||reg||1
